From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:19:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: report the tx rate of single-frame confirmations

get_station takes a station's tx bitrate from last_tx_rate_config, but
only the burst confirmation path (siwifi_txdatacfm_burst, used with
NEW_SCHEDULE) stores it. This build confirms frames one at a time
through siwifi_txdatacfm, which keeps the firmware's rateinfo and
leaves last_tx_rate_config at zero: non-HT, legacy index 0. Every
station, on either side of a link, showed a tx bitrate of 1.0 MBit/s
whatever rate the firmware used.

Store the rate config in siwifi_txdatacfm as well, as the driver in
Siflower's 1806 SDK does.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_tx.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_tx.c b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_tx.c
index 54415d1..416db38 100644
--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_tx.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_tx.c
@@ -1669,6 +1669,7 @@ int siwifi_txdatacfm(void *pthis, void *host_id)
     if (sw_txhdr->siwifi_sta && !(sw_txhdr->desc.host.flags & TXU_CNTRL_MGMT)
             && !is_multicast_ether_addr((const u8 *)&txhdr->sw_hdr->desc.host.eth_dest_addr)){
         sw_txhdr->siwifi_sta->stats.last_tx_info = txhdr->hw_hdr.cfm.rateinfo;
+        sw_txhdr->siwifi_sta->stats.last_tx_rate_config = txhdr->hw_hdr.cfm.rate_config;
     }
 #ifdef CONFIG_VDR_HW
     vendor_hook_txdata(sw_txhdr);
